# Supreme program control

Before substantial work (features, architecture, security, production, product modules, infrastructure, major GTM), read:

- `docs/SUPREME-MASTER-PUNCH-LIST.md`
- `docs/SUPREME-PROGRAM-STATE.md`
- `docs/SUPREME-PRODUCT-OPERATING-RULES.md`
- any ACCEPTED ADR that applies

State the current punch-list item, status, verified SHA, dependencies, and next authorized item.

If the request skips an unfinished numbered dependency, say so before implementing. Do not start #9 or later unless program state authorizes it.

Do not merge `main`, deploy production, change production DNS, or declare production-ready without explicit program authorization.

Trivial typo or comment-only edits do not need a full program recitation.

Accepted ADRs control. If a request conflicts with an ACCEPTED ADR, stop and name the conflict.

Do not change PASS / PARTIAL / FAIL / BLOCKED without evidence. Hosted gates require hosted proof. Marketing preview pages are not implementation.
